hey what's up guys my name is samuel  leeds i'm a property investor and in  this video i'm going to be talking about  the pros and the cons versus buying  flats as investments apartments and just  straight houses and homes is it better  to buy flats or houses what gives you  the best return on investment and should  you consider flats when you're looking  to buy your first property investment so  here are my overall thoughts  there's no right or wrong answer i  personally prefer  houses and i'll tell you why in a moment  unless the flats are particularly unique  and  let me explain why so firstly the good  things about buying flats the reason  that people are attracted to buying  flats is that they're cheap so  you can buy flats in the midlands around  birmingham for like 30 40 50 000 pounds  and they are in decent areas they do  rent out okay and i think the fact that  they're so cheap really does attract  people to want to buy them secondly the  good thing about flats is it's really  easy to do your research on a flat  because especially if it's in like a  block  there's so many comparables so you can  see this one sold for 50 grand this one  sold for 55. this one sold for 53 and  you can look and you can see i'm right  with all the comparables so working out  whether you're getting a good deal and  working out what the rent is going to be  because there's so many like-for-like  comparables in that same block it makes  it really easy to do your research and  the third reason is because there's  really low maintenance so the garden's  communal if there's a garden at all  everything's all shared and communal the  building itself it's not your building  to have to maintain so you usually with  flats and i've got flats and i've also  got houses and there are um pretty low  maintenance the repairs and things i  tend to be quite low with flats so  that's the good  the bad so in my experience and i'm not  saying this is always the case because  it does depend on different factors but  i don't own loads of flats but the flats  that i did buy in 2009 2010 almost 10  years ago  haven't hardly appreciated in value at  all they've not gone up in value and i  think they did go up in value in the 90s  flats absolutely went crazy i think that  was partly because of the series and i'm  totally serious when i say this the  series friends  and they're all living and it's like a  cool lifestyle they're living in  apartments what happened in new york  everyone wanted to live in an apartment  and then um usually england copies and  follows america in some instances and  then suddenly it became really trendy  like in the 90s and everyone wanted to  live in an apartment but then when i  bought an apartment in 2009 i bought a  few  um  that's kind of died now everyone wants  houses and i've found in the last decade  apartments have become less and less  popular so the appreciation on them has  been very small compared to houses so  that's a bit of an egg and and to be  honest i can't see  i just can't see that flats are going to  rock it in value unless they're unique  and they're in a really good location or  they're they're um very special they're  penthouses or they're part of something  amazing i just can't see that they're  going to give the same capital  appreciation as houses will another  problem with flats is  i think if you wanted to sell a flat  people do not buy flats in 2019 to live  in what they do is they rent a flat  and then they save up and then they buy  a house so if you've got flats and  you're trying to sell them you're going  to struggle to sell them to  people that are going to actually live  in them homeowners you're going to sell  them to investors and if you're selling  them to investors investors never want  to pay the full price they want to get  squeezed the lowest so again wanting to  sell them afterwards unless you're  prepared to sell them quite low i think  you're going to struggle to sell them  but the biggest problem i have with  flats the number one reason i tell  people not to buy flats and to be  careful  is because of the service charge and  ground rent what does that mean because  you don't own the land because if you  just buy a flat in inside a building you  don't own the building you don't own the  land you're just buying  that apartment so what that means is  that means that you have to pay a  service charge and a ground rent to the  person who does own the land  and to keep everything like the communal  areas all okay and the scary thing about  flats is you cannot predict what that  service charge or ground rent might be  in the future so they can they can  change it sometimes it might just be a  couple hundred pound a year sometimes it  can be a couple thousand so if you are  gonna buy a flat just make sure that you  do your proper research and you know  exactly what your roi return on  investment is going to be and you've  included knocking off the ground rent  and the service charges so get that  information it's really important  because it can be a lot and it can you  can buy a flat and you can rent it out  for 600 pound a month and and once  you've paid your mortgage new management  you might be left with 300 pound a month  but if your service charge and ground  rank come down to 600 pounds a year  that's two months rent  totally wiped out just because it's a  flat and not a house so that's something  you really need to be careful of so i  think overall my advice would be  flats are okay  apartments that's the posh word for  staying flat they're okay but if you're  gonna buy one number one make sure that  you're aware that you probably aren't  gonna own the land  secondly be really careful on what the  ground rate and the service charge are  so you can work out your figures  properly and thirdly  make sure that it's not it's attractive  make sure that i mean make sure that  there's something special or something  unique so that when you go to want to  resell it you're gonna not have such a  hard time rather than just being like a  little tiny studio with 50 others the  same in a big block i'd be a bit careful  of those properties so i hope you found  that video useful my big suggestion if  you're going to go down flats i have to  say this is  if you buy the whole building and then  convert it into flats that's totally  different that's totally different  because then you own the land you've got  complete control and another good thing  about flats that you could do is you  could buy them and rent them out as  serviced accommodation so that could be  another reason where they where they  could be really profitable so it is gray  it's not black and white but i hope that  helps you when you're doing your  research  something i really suggest that you  check out is i've done a video called  what makes a good property investment  which just talks about all the things  you need to look for the basics when  you're before you buy any property  investment you can check that out  there's a video right here also if you  want to spend two days actually doing  this finding deals getting up your  laptops i'd really suggest that you come  down to the property investors crash  course on the house free on me you can  get tickets right here and don't forget  to subscribe over here as well

